 a basis and the dimension of the subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^4$ spanned by the vectors $(1,1,2,4)$, $(2,-1,-5,2)$, $(1,-1,-4,0)$ and $(2,1,1,6)$.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/aa43e1e4f65a26a0a3a7/q-10-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,382,1405,102]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"aa43e1e4f65a26a0a3a7-q-11","number":"4B","markdown":"Let $U=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}a & -a\\\\ b & -b\\end{bmatrix}: a,b\\in\\mathbb{R}\\right\\}$ and $W=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}a & -a\\\\ 0 & b\\end{bmatrix}: a,b\\in\\mathbb{R}\\right\\}$\n\nFind a basis and the dimension of the subspaces (i) $U\\cap W$ (ii) $U+W$.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/aa43e1e4f65a26a0a3a7/q-11-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,476,1405,153]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"aa43e1e4f65a26a0a3a7-q-12","number":"4C","markdown":"Let $T:\\mathbb{R}^3\\to\\mathbb{R}^2$ be a linear transformation defined by\n\n$$\nT(x,y,z)=(5x-3y+z,\\ 2z+4y).\n$$\n\nFind $\\operatorname{rank}(T)$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(T)$.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/aa43e1e4f65a26a0a3a7/page-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,0,1405,1989]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"aa43e1e4f65a26a0a3a7-q-13","number":"5A","markdown":"Find the matrix representation of the linear transformation\n\n$T:\\mathbb{R}^2\\to\\mathbb{R}^2$ defined by $T(x,y)=(x-3y,\\ 2x+4y)$ relative to the basis $S=\\{(1,2),(1,-1)\\}$. Hence find the coordinate vector of $T(1,1)$ relative to the basis $S$.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/aa43e1e4f65a26a0a3a7/q-13-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,828,1405,173]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"aa43e1e4f65a26a0a3a7-q-14","number":"5B","markdown":"Find the cosine of the angle between two matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4\\\\ 5 & 6 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\